<title>USA: First Midwest Bancorp to buy back shares.</title>
<headline>First Midwest Bancorp to buy back shares.</headline>
<dateline>ITASCA, Ill. 1996-11-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>First Midwest Bancorp Inc said Wednesday it plans to repurchase up to 900,000 shares, or 6.6 percent, of its outstanding common stock.</p>
<p>The company also said it plans to repurchase an unspecified additional number of shares over the next year in conjunction with stock option and employee benefit plans.  </p>
<p>The $3.1 billion asset bank holding company said the transactiosn would be made in the open market or through privately negotiated transactions.</p>
<p>First Midwest shares rose 1/2 to 34 on Nasdaq Wednesday.</p>
<p>--Reuters Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787</p>
</text>
